# Portfolio conventions

Flask + Jinja. Routes in `app.py`: `/` → `templates/index.html`, `/thoughts` → `templates/thoughts.html`, `/work/<slug>` → `templates/case.html`. Work data is `case_files.py`. All CSS is `public/style.css`. Static files are served from `public/`. Design details live in `DESIGN_CONTEXT.md`.

## Match the existing visual style

Minimal, editorial, dark. Reuse classes and tokens in `public/style.css`. Do not add a component library, Tailwind, icons, or decorative chrome.

- Fonts: `--font-display` (DM Serif Display) for the name, page and section titles, project and post titles, pull quotes; `--font-body` (Lato 400) for everything else. No monospace. Sentence case; no uppercase or letter-spaced labels.
- Color: background `--color-bg` `#0F1117`; text `--color-text-heading`, `--color-text-body`, `--color-text-muted`; hairlines `--color-line`. One accent, `--color-accent` `#EA580C`, used only for availability ("Open to APM roles"), hover and focus.
- Layout: `.container` (max 1200px, padding 24px). Screenshots sit in `.case-window` (1px border, 8px radius). Links are underlined text with `.case-chapter__cta`, never pills or buttons.
- The homepage Work section is a compact index of `.work-row`s (screenshot or key metric, title, deck, meta line, links). Long write-ups, narratives and pull quotes belong on the `/work/<slug>` case study pages, not the homepage.
- No numbering, captions, badges, window chrome, shadows, gradients, textures, or scroll or load animations. The hero chart (`figure.hero-gap`) is the one animated moment; don't add others.
- Keep `:focus-visible` outlines. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

```html
<!-- ✅ reuse the frame and the text link -->
<div class="case-window">...</div>
<a class="case-chapter__cta" href="/work/slug">Read case study</a>
<!-- ❌ a new card system or pill button -->
<div class="project-card">...</div>
```

## Never invent content

Metrics, quotes, results, dates, and links must already exist in the templates, `case_files.py`, or the Substack feed. If a value is missing, show a visible `TODO:` placeholder and tell the user what to supply. Never link a file in `public/` that isn't there, and never present illustrative or concept figures (like First SIP's) as real results.

```html
<!-- ❌ -->
<p>Raised retention 40%.</p>
<!-- ✅ -->
<p>TODO: add the outcome for this case.</p>
```

## Keep changes scoped

Edit only files the task needs. Do not refactor unrelated CSS, templates, or data.

## Semantic HTML and keyboard access

Use real headings, landmarks, and buttons. Images need meaningful `alt`. Decorative separators stay `aria-hidden="true"`. Controls must work from the keyboard and keep the existing focus ring.

## After each task

List every file changed, and anything the user still needs to provide (copy, images, links, PDFs).
